.TH INZONE-TOOLS 1 "2026-10-04" "inzone-linux 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
inzone-tools \- initialize INZONE user configuration and prepare DSP assets
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B inzone-tools setup --assets-from
.I DIRECTORY
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B inzone-tools setup --download
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B inzone-tools --help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B inzone-tools
provides package setup, asset extraction, source installation, and diagnostic
commands. Use
.B --help
for the complete command reference.
.PP
The Debian package supplies application executables, the DSP plugin, desktop
integration, and configuration templates. Sony DSP assets are prepared
separately for each desktop user.
.SH PACKAGE SETUP
.B setup
initializes user configuration through the existing transactional installer.
It preserves saved profile state and does not replace a locally installed
.B inzone-profile
executable. The automatic profile service uses the packaged executable.
.PP
Setup must run as the desktop user without
.BR sudo .
It does not restart audio services. Apply a profile with
.B inzone-profile
after setup completes.
.TP
.BI "--assets-from " DIRECTORY
Read an existing prepared checkout or asset cache. The directory must contain
.B assets/
and
.BR analysis/payload/ .
This mode does not download files.
.TP
.B --download
Explicitly download and verify the pinned INZONE Hub installer and prepare
its audio assets in the user cache. Extraction requires 7-Zip and .NET 10.
The command obtains the pinned ilspycmd version when it is missing.
Windows executables are not executed.
.TP
.BI "--home " DIRECTORY
Use the specified desktop home directory. It must match the current process's
runtime home and belong to the current user.
.TP
.BI "--resources " DIRECTORY
Use configuration templates, documentation, and the DSP plugin from the
specified package setup resource directory. The default is resolved relative
to the installed executable.
.PP
Exactly one of
.B --assets-from
and
.B --download
is required. Setup never downloads assets implicitly.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/inzone-linux/setup/
Package setup resources.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/inzone-linux/setup/
Default download and extraction cache. An absolute
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
changes the cache base directory.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/inzone-linux/backups/
Backups retained when existing user configuration is replaced.
.SH EXAMPLES
Reuse assets from a prepared source checkout:
.PP
.nf
inzone-tools setup --assets-from /path/to/inzone-linux
.fi
.PP
Explicitly acquire the pinned assets:
.PP
.nf
inzone-tools setup --download
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR inzone-profile (1),
.BR inzone-gui (1)
